select i.team_id, i.id, $il$Oliver$il$, '2026-09-17T13:30:00.000Z'::timestamptz,
$il$SECOND INSTANCE, AND A HARDER ONE. Marcel de Groot, CEO Vodafone Germany, P-record under Vodafone Germany. He has disabled communication on LinkedIn entirely: no connection request possible and no message possible. Oliver's question was simply how to log it, and today there is nowhere correct to put it.

WHAT HAS HAPPENED INSTEAD IS THE PROBLEM THIS ITEM PREDICTS. His Outreach Status reads Not relevant. He is the chief executive of a target operator. He is extremely relevant and simply unreachable on one channel. A channel fact has been written into a relevance field, and the cost is that every future reader, human or agent, will skip him for the wrong reason and never revisit it.

SO THE ENUM NEEDS THE CLOSED CASE, not just the conditional one. Rebuy's Daniel Freudenberger could still be invited if we had his email. This profile accepts nothing at all. Two distinct values:
  Connection request: not available, profile does not accept invitations
  LinkedIn message: not available, profile has messaging disabled
With both set, the derived answer is LinkedIn closed, and the next step has to come from somewhere else rather than the contact being parked.

AND THE FALLBACK IS A COMPANY LEVEL ANSWER, NOT A CONTACT LEVEL ONE. For a CEO of an operator the right move was never a cold connection request anyway. When every channel on a contact is closed, the system should point at the company and ask who else there is worth approaching, which is the acceptance coverage rule. Closing a contact must not quietly close the company.$il$
