$il$FOURTH INSTANCE, Kristjan Nemvalts at Upgreat, P694, Estonia. It reads PREVIOUS DRAFTS 1, which makes it four out of four. That correlation is now strong enough to test directly, and it should be tested before anything is changed: approve a draft that has NEVER been revised, so PREVIOUS DRAFTS is absent. If it succeeds, the revision number is being counted from previous drafts only and that is the bug. If it fails too, it is the double invocation seen on the topi card. Five minutes either way.

The counters still balance: 63 pending and 14 approved becomes 61 and 16, with Rejected unchanged at 21. So approvals are still saving and only the revision snapshot is failing. Four instances in, nothing has been lost.$il$
