select i.team_id, i.id, $il$Claude$il$, '2026-09-17T15:20:00.000Z'::timestamptz,
$il$17 Sept, THIS IS NOT A GERMAN PROBLEM, IT IS A DRAFTING PROBLEM. The English draft to Louis Salzman-Le Goff at WeFix contains we can give all your clients ON month of free insurance cover, for ONE month, and which is a great USB to buy on your website, for USP. A wrong word and a wrong acronym in consecutive lines, in English, on a P2 contact in France.

Neither was caught. The lint on that card scored 85 and did flag a terminology rule, Use Partner not client, so it is checking something. It is not checking whether the words are the right words. Title and scope of this item widened accordingly.

USB for USP is the kind of error that reads as careless rather than as a typo, because the reader cannot tell which word was meant. Worth saying because it argues for a spell and sense pass on every draft in whatever language it is written, not a German specific rule.$il$
