insert into public.improvements (team_id, item_key, title, category, owner, priority, status, raised_by, created_at, build_wave, blocks, blocked_by, done_by, done_at, pinned, hidden, seen_by, detail, notes)
values ((select id from public.teams limit 1), $il$i099$il$, $il$A contact cannot be moved to a different company from the front end$il$, $il$Lovable UI$il$, $il$Brad$il$, $il$must$il$, $il$open$il$, $il$Oliver$il$, '2026-09-17T12:50:00.000Z'::timestamptz, 5, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], null, null, false, false, $il${}$il$::jsonb,
$il$Oliver cannot move a contact to a different company from the front end. When a contact is attached to the wrong company, there is no way to correct it where he is standing.

THE RECORD HE FOUND IT ON IS A GOOD EXAMPLE OF WHY IT MATTERS. Ben Beasley sits under Vodafone Germany. His country is UK, his city is London, and his own background note reads Global Director of Partnerships at Vodafone, group level UK, linked to C307 Vodafone Germany. So a UK group level person is filed under the German operating company.

THAT IS NOT A TIDINESS PROBLEM. The company a contact hangs off decides several things that then run automatically:
  Territory and owner. UK is Jack's, DACH is Oliver's. A wrong company puts a contact in the wrong person's book.
  Monday suppression. If the company is worked in monday, the contact should not appear in a lake worklist at all.
  Scoring and prioritisation. The company carries the devices, the category and the score that decide whether its people are worth a connection request.
  Grouping and duplicate detection, which read the parent company.

WHAT IS NEEDED

1. A Company field on the contact that can be changed, with a type to search picker. The same picker as the new contact dialog in i046, so there is one way to choose a company in the app rather than two.

2. The picker must show every company, including ones worked in monday. i046 found it silently hides them, which is how spusu looked missing. If a company is suppressed, show it and label it suppressed rather than leaving it out.

3. Moving a contact keeps its history. Touches, drafts, notes and next action travel with the person, not with the old company link.

4. Record the move. Who changed it, from what, to what, and when, on the contact timeline. This is the same gap as i076, where notes are saved undated and unattributed.

5. Warn before a move that changes something consequential: a different country or owner, or a move into a company that is worked in monday. Do not block it, say what will follow.

BUILD THE SIMPLE MOVE FIRST. i058 asks for a contact to belong to more than one company, which is the fuller answer. Even with that, one company has to be the primary, and this is the control that sets it. It is also a prerequisite for the group work in i047, because fixing a group is mostly moving people between its members.

AND THE DESTINATION MAY NOT EXIST YET. Oliver's point on Ben Beasley is that he works at Vodafone GROUP level, not at Vodafone Germany. If there is no Vodafone Group record in the lake, a reassignment control on its own does not solve his case: he needs a parent entity to be moved to. So this lands next to i047. The picker must therefore be able to create a company inline, as i046 already asks for the new contact dialog, otherwise the answer to a wrong parent is a second wrong parent.

THE GENERAL RULE UNDERNEATH IT. A person who operates at group level should hang off the group, with the operating companies as its children, not off whichever subsidiary happened to be in the lake first. Getting that right is what makes the group rollup in i047 mean anything, because otherwise a group's contacts are scattered across its subsidiaries by accident of import.$il$,
$il$THE WORKAROUND TODAY IS TO ASK BRAD OR EDIT THE DATABASE, which means a correction that takes five seconds to see takes a day to apply, and most of them simply do not get made. That is how a lake fills with contacts filed under the wrong entity.

IT WILL COME UP OFTEN WITH GROUPS. Vodafone Germany against Vodafone group, mobilezone against Sparhandy, asgoodasnew against Save Group: every one of those is a case where the right company for a person is a judgement, and the first guess is frequently wrong. i047 and i068 are both about getting the group structure right, and neither is much use if the people cannot be moved once the structure is fixed.

TWO OTHER THINGS ON THE SAME CARD, NEITHER RAISED BY OLIVER, BOTH WORTH A GLANCE.
  The next action date reads 19 May 2026, four months in the past, while Outreach Status reads Parked and the cooldown runs until 25 February 2027. Three fields describing the same plan and none of them agree. Nothing surfaces an overdue next action, so it just sits there.
  Connection Status reads Withdrawn, which under the six month re-invite cooldown means this contact cannot be re-approached until February 2027 anyway. Worth confirming the cooldown date is derived from the withdrawal rather than typed, because if it is typed it will drift.$il$);

